Q: What happens when a client calls your Spring Boot API?

Example: GET https://api.example.com/users/1

1) DNS  
api.example.com → IP address

2) TCP connect  
Client opens TCP to server IP:443 (HTTPS)

3) TLS handshake  
Certificates/keys → encrypted channel

4) HTTP request  
GET /users/1 HTTP/1.1  
Host: api.example.com  
Authorization: Bearer ...

5) Server stack  
Load balancer / reverse proxy (optional) → Tomcat/Netty → Spring DispatcherServlet → Controller → Service → DB

6) HTTP response  
200 OK + JSON body

7) TCP may stay open (keep-alive) for next requests

Interview tip:
Separate **transport problems** (DNS/TCP/TLS/timeouts) from **app problems** (4xx/5xx business logic).
